From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:36:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: expect no SA Query of a non-AP MLD after a channel
 switch

After a channel switch, hostapd_event_ch_switch() marks each OCV station
of the BSS and disconnects it after 15 s unless an SA Query Request
arrives on that link. A non-AP MLD gets the channel from protected Beacon
frames of the setup link (IEEE Std 802.11be-2024 12.2.10), and
wpa_supplicant sends no SA Query for a switch on a link other than the
association link. Mark no non-AP MLD.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
@@ -1476,6 +1476,11 @@ void hostapd_event_ch_switch(struct host
 		bool check_sa_query = false;
 
 		for (sta = hapd->sta_list; sta; sta = sta->next) {
+			/* An MLD validates a channel change from the Beacon
+			 * frames of the setup link (802.11be 12.2.10) */
+			if (ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta))
+				continue;
+
 			if (wpa_auth_uses_ocv(sta->wpa_sm) &&
 			    !(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_WNM_SLEEP_MODE)) {
 				sta->post_csa_sa_query = 1;
